---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="For Organizations | Ethnoir"
  description="Ethnoir works with organizations shaping entrepreneurship and venture development to examine current conditions and make better-informed decisions."
>
  <!-- A. OPENING -->
  <section class="bg-parchment" style="padding: var(--space-md) 0 var(--space-2xl) 0;">
    <div class="container grid-12">
      <!-- Masterhead Headline -->
      <div class="col-12 md-col-11" style="padding-top: 0; padding-bottom: var(--space-xl);">
        <h1 class="voice-1" style="font-size: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5rem); margin: 0; line-height: 1.05; letter-spacing: -0.02em; color: var(--color-tidal-ink);">
          Better support begins with a clearer understanding of the ventures and people it is meant to serve.
        </h1>
      </div>
      
      <!-- Offset Intro Block -->
      <div class="col-12 grid-12" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--color-strong-boundary); padding-top: var(--space-lg);">
        <div class="col-12 md-col-4" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-md);">
          <span class="voice-3" style="color: var(--color-muted-slate);">Institutional Orientation</span>
        </div>
        <div class="col-12 md-col-7">
          <p class="voice-2" style="font-size: 1.375rem; line-height: 1.4; color: var(--color-tidal-ink); margin-bottom: var(--space-md);">
            Ethnoir works with organizations shaping entrepreneurship and venture development to examine current conditions, clarify the question at hand and make better-informed decisions about direction and support.
          </p>
          <p class="voice-2" style="font-size: 1.125rem; color: var(--color-muted-slate); margin-bottom: var(--space-xl); line-height: 1.6;">
            This work may be relevant when an organization is developing an initiative, reconsidering an existing approach or trying to understand where an existing approach may be creating friction, leaving important questions unresolved or not working as intended.
          </p>
          <div class="actions-group">
            <a href="/contact" class="btn-primary" style="background-color: var(--color-tidal-ink); color: var(--color-porcelain);">Discuss a venture-development challenge</a>
            <a href="/our-work" class="link-secondary">View Our Work &rarr;</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- B. WHO THIS PAGE IS FOR -->
  <section class="bg-porcelain chapter chapter-moderate-spacing" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--color-strong-boundary);">
    <div class="container grid-12">
      <div class="col-12 md-col-4" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--color-tidal-ink); padding-top: var(--space-sm);">
        <h2 class="voice-1" style="font-size: 1.75rem;">For organizations whose work shapes venture development</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="col-12 md-col-7-offset" style="padding-top: var(--space-sm);">
        <p class="voice-2" style="font-size: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: var(--space-md);">
          Ethnoir welcomes conversations with entrepreneurship-support organizations, universities, foundations, nonprofits, public institutions and other organizations whose work materially shapes entrepreneurship and venture development.
        </p>
        <div style="padding-left: var(--space-md); border-left: 1px solid var(--color-quiet-rule);">
          <p class="voice-2">
            The organization does not need to be a business. The essential connection is that its decisions, programs or support arrangements affect people exploring, building, operating or changing entrepreneurial ventures.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- C. QUESTIONS THAT MAY FIT -->
  <section class="bg-quiet-sand chapter chapter-large-spacing">
    <div class="container grid-12">
      <div class="col-12 md-col-4" style="position: sticky; top: 120px; align-self: start;">
        <span class="voice-3">Questions that may fit</span>
        <h2 class="voice-1" style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem); margin-bottom: var(--space-md);">What is your organization trying to understand?</h2>
        <p class="voice-2" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);">
          A conversation with Ethnoir may be useful when your organization is asking:
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="col-12 md-col-7-offset">
        <div style="border-top: 1px solid var(--color-strong-boundary);">
          <div class="thin-rule-x" style="padding: var(--space-md) 0;">
            <p class="voice-1" style="font-size: 1.5rem; margin: 0; color: var(--color-tidal-ink);">What are participating entrepreneurs actually navigating?</p>
          </div>
          <div class="thin-rule-x" style="padding: var(--space-md) 0;">
            <p class="voice-1" style="font-size: 1.5rem; margin: 0; color: var(--color-tidal-ink);">Which venture conditions matter most to the decision or program at hand?</p>
          </div>
          <div class="thin-rule-x" style="padding: var(--space-md) 0;">
            <p class="voice-1" style="font-size: 1.5rem; margin: 0; color: var(--color-tidal-ink);">What assumptions about stage, growth, funding or readiness are shaping our approach?</p>
          </div>
          <div class="thin-rule-x" style="padding: var(--space-md) 0;">
            <p class="voice-1" style="font-size: 1.5rem; margin: 0; color: var(--color-tidal-ink);">How are people experiencing and using the support we provide?</p>
          </div>
          <div class="thin-rule-x" style="padding: var(--space-md) 0;">
            <p class="voice-1" style="font-size: 1.5rem; margin: 0; color: var(--color-tidal-ink);">Where are participants encountering confusion, friction or demands that make the support difficult to use?</p>
          </div>
          <div style="padding: var(--space-md) 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-strong-boundary);">
            <p class="voice-1" style="font-size: 1.5rem; margin: 0; color: var(--color-tidal-ink);">What does the available evidence support, and what may warrant reconsideration or further investigation?</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div style="margin-top: var(--space-lg); padding: var(--space-md); background-color: var(--color-parchment);">
          <p class="voice-2" style="margin: 0; font-style: italic;">
            Ethnoir does not assume that every issue requires a new program, a more complex tool or a larger intervention. Sometimes the useful next step is to define the question more carefully or gather better information.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- D. HOW ETHNOIR APPROACHES THE WORK -->
  <section class="bg-parchment chapter chapter-moderate-spacing">
    <div class="container grid-12">
      <div class="col-12" style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);">
        <span class="voice-3">How Ethnoir approaches the work</span>
        <h2 class="voice-1" style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem); max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; line-height: 1.1;">
          Start with the challenge, not a predetermined service.
        </h2>
      </div>
      <div class="col-12" style="max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto;">
        <p class="voice-2" style="font-size: 1.25rem; text-align: center; margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);">
          The form of the work should follow the question—not the other way around.
        </p>
        
        <div style="border: 1px solid var(--color-quiet-rule); padding: var(--space-lg); background-color: var(--color-porcelain);">
          <p class="voice-2" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-md); font-weight: 500;">Ethnoir begins by understanding:</p>
          <ul style="list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0 0 var(--space-lg) 0;">
            <li style="margin-bottom: var(--space-sm); padding-left: var(--space-md); position: relative;">
              <span style="position: absolute; left: 0; color: var(--color-strong-boundary);">&mdash;</span>
              the decision or challenge the organization is facing;
            </li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: var(--space-sm); padding-left: var(--space-md); position: relative;">
              <span style="position: absolute; left: 0; color: var(--color-strong-boundary);">&mdash;</span>
              the people and ventures affected;
            </li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: var(--space-sm); padding-left: var(--space-md); position: relative;">
              <span style="position: absolute; left: 0; color: var(--color-strong-boundary);">&mdash;</span>
              the purpose of the support or initiative;
            </li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: var(--space-sm); padding-left: var(--space-md); position: relative;">
              <span style="position: absolute; left: 0; color: var(--color-strong-boundary);">&mdash;</span>
              the information already available; and
            </li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 0; padding-left: var(--space-md); position: relative;">
              <span style="position: absolute; left: 0; color: var(--color-strong-boundary);">&mdash;</span>
              the assumptions, constraints and uncertainties involved.
            </li>
          </ul>
          
          <div style="border-top: 1px solid var(--color-quiet-rule); padding-top: var(--space-md);">
            <p class="voice-2" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);">
              The objective is not to manufacture certainty or impose a universal model. It is to create a clearer, better-informed basis for decisions about venture direction and support.
            </p>
            <p class="voice-2" style="color: var(--color-muted-slate);">
              From there, we can determine whether Ethnoir may be a useful fit.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- E. WHAT ETHNOIR BRINGS -->
  <section class="bg-porcelain chapter chapter-moderate-spacing" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--color-quiet-rule);">
    <div class="container grid-12">
      <div class="col-12 md-col-4">
        <span class="voice-3">What Ethnoir brings</span>
      </div>
      <div class="col-12 md-col-7">
        <h2 class="voice-1" style="font-size: 2rem; margin-bottom: var(--space-md);">Connecting venture conditions, judgment and support</h2>
        <p class="voice-2" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-md);">
          Ethnoir’s current work brings together the ability to organize relevant information, develop a careful interpretation of current conditions, help frame what may deserve attention and learn from the implementation of venture-development work.
        </p>
        <p class="voice-2" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-md);">
          Ethnoir has also designed structured founder-facing support connecting a clear purpose and participant population with a coherent sequence, practical activities and appropriate forms of support.
        </p>
        <p class="voice-2" style="color: var(--color-muted-slate);">
          For institutional work, these abilities provide a foundation for examining a clearly defined entrepreneurship or venture-development challenge. The appropriate contribution depends on the question and begins with careful scoping.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- F. PROPOSED INSTITUTIONAL APPLICATION -->
  <section class="bg-quiet-sand chapter chapter-large-spacing" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--color-strong-boundary);">
    <div class="container">
      <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);">
        <span class="voice-3" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-sm); display: block;">Proposed Institutional Application</span>
        <h2 class="voice-1" style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.5rem); margin-bottom: var(--space-md);">A clearer view of participant needs</h2>
        <p class="voice-2" style="max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto; font-size: 1.125rem;">
          Ethnoir is developing an institutional application of its venture-readiness approach designed to help entrepreneurship-support organizations understand participant needs, segment founders, inform appropriate program placement and referral decisions, and examine capability change. <span style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-tidal-ink); padding-bottom: 2px;">It has not yet been tested with a partner organization.</span>
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- 3 Areas -->
      <div class="grid-12" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--color-strong-boundary); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-strong-boundary); margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);">
        <div class="col-12 md-col-4 border-right-md" style="padding: var(--space-lg) var(--space-sm);">
          <h3 class="voice-1" style="font-size: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);">Better founder segmentation</h3>
          <p class="voice-2" style="font-size: 0.9375rem; color: var(--color-muted-slate);">
            A carefully bounded view of readiness stages and primary constraints could help a partner distinguish materially different participant needs without assuming one pathway fits everyone.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-12 md-col-4 border-right-md" style="padding: var(--space-lg) var(--space-sm);">
          <h3 class="voice-1" style="font-size: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);">More appropriate program placement and referrals</h3>
          <p class="voice-2" style="font-size: 0.9375rem; color: var(--color-muted-slate);">
            Findings could inform program placement or referral pathways when used within an appropriately scoped decision process. This has not been validated for eligibility, selection or resource-allocation decisions.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-12 md-col-4" style="padding: var(--space-lg) var(--space-sm);">
          <h3 class="voice-1" style="font-size: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);">Clearer evidence of founder capability change</h3>
          <p class="voice-2" style="font-size: 0.9375rem; color: var(--color-muted-slate);">
            Follow-up evidence could help a partner examine capability change and remaining constraints. It would not, by itself, establish program effectiveness or institutional outcomes.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Partner Application Process -->
      <div style="max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto var(--space-xl);">
        <h3 class="voice-3" style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);">What a partner application could look like</h3>
        <div style="border-left: 1px solid var(--color-tidal-ink); padding-left: var(--space-lg);">
          <ol style="list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0;">
            <li style="position: relative; margin-bottom: var(--space-md);">
              <span style="position: absolute; left: calc(-1 * var(--space-lg) - 0.5rem); background: var(--color-quiet-sand); padding: 4px 0; font-family: var(--font-heading); color: var(--color-tidal-ink);">1.</span>
              <p class="voice-2">Founders complete the Venture Readiness Check-In or another appropriately scoped diagnostic process.</p>
            </li>
            <li style="position: relative; margin-bottom: var(--space-md);">
              <span style="position: absolute; left: calc(-1 * var(--space-lg) - 0.5rem); background: var(--color-quiet-sand); padding: 4px 0; font-family: var(--font-heading); color: var(--color-tidal-ink);">2.</span>
              <p class="voice-2">Ethnoir examines readiness stages and primary constraints.</p>
            </li>
            <li style="position: relative; margin-bottom: var(--space-md);">
              <span style="position: absolute; left: calc(-1 * var(--space-lg) - 0.5rem); background: var(--color-quiet-sand); padding: 4px 0; font-family: var(--font-heading); color: var(--color-tidal-ink);">3.</span>
              <p class="voice-2">The partner receives a bounded view of participant segments and needs.</p>
            </li>
            <li style="position: relative; margin-bottom: var(--space-md);">
              <span style="position: absolute; left: calc(-1 * var(--space-lg) - 0.5rem); background: var(--color-quiet-sand); padding: 4px 0; font-family: var(--font-heading); color: var(--color-tidal-ink);">4.</span>
              <p class="voice-2">Findings can inform program placement or referral pathways.</p>
            </li>
            <li style="position: relative; margin-bottom: var(--space-md);">
              <span style="position: absolute; left: calc(-1 * var(--space-lg) - 0.5rem); background: var(--color-quiet-sand); padding: 4px 0; font-family: var(--font-heading); color: var(--color-tidal-ink);">5.</span>
              <p class="voice-2">Targeted support can be selected or designed.</p>
            </li>
            <li style="position: relative;">
              <span style="position: absolute; left: calc(-1 * var(--space-lg) - 0.5rem); background: var(--color-quiet-sand); padding: 4px 0; font-family: var(--font-heading); color: var(--color-tidal-ink);">6.</span>
              <p class="voice-2">Follow-up evidence can examine capability change and remaining constraints.</p>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Limitation Statement -->
      <div style="background-color: var(--color-parchment); border: 1px solid var(--color-quiet-rule); padding: var(--space-lg); text-align: center; max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto var(--space-lg);">
        <p class="voice-2" style="margin: 0; color: var(--color-tidal-ink);">
          This is a proposed institutional application. Ethnoir has tested founder-facing diagnostic and implementation support through the Venture Readiness Lab, but has not yet shown that this institutional application improves referrals, placement, resource allocation, partner performance or organization-level capability change.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- External Context Placeholder -->
      <div style="max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; text-align: center; border: 1px dashed var(--color-strong-boundary); padding: var(--space-md);">
        <span class="voice-3">External context — evidence pending verification</span>
        <p class="voice-2" style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--color-muted-slate); margin: 0;">
          [Placeholder: verified Federal Reserve evidence about founder and business-support challenges may be added here once the source, wording and relevance are confirmed. It must not be presented as evidence that Ethnoir’s model works.]
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- G. CURRENT EVIDENCE -->
  <section class="bg-parchment chapter chapter-moderate-spacing" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--color-quiet-rule);">
    <div class="container grid-12">
      <div class="col-12 md-col-4">
        <span class="voice-3">Current evidence</span>
        <h2 class="voice-1" style="font-size: 2rem; margin-bottom: var(--space-md);">Learning through direct work with founders</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="col-12 md-col-8">
        <p class="voice-2" style="font-size: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: var(--space-md);">
          In 2026, Ethnoir designed and delivered the Venture Readiness Lab, a six-week founder-facing pilot.
        </p>
        
        <div class="stats-grid" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-md);">
          <div class="stat-block">
            <div class="stat-huge">06</div>
            <div class="stat-caption">weeks</div>
          </div>
          <div class="stat-block">
            <div class="stat-huge">06</div>
            <div class="stat-caption">active founders<br/><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--color-muted-slate);">reached the final session</span></div>
          </div>
          <div class="stat-block">
            <div class="stat-huge">05</div>
            <div class="stat-caption">active participants<br/><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--color-muted-slate);">with structural business deliverables independently reviewed and confirmed</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <div style="max-width: 720px;">
          <p class="voice-2" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-md);">
            The Lab also generated practical learning about how founders interpret common business concepts, translate identified issues into usable responses and engage with program materials, technology and implementation demands.
          </p>
          <p class="voice-2" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-lg); color: var(--color-muted-slate);">
            Ethnoir’s direct organizational evidence is currently strongest in founder-facing work. The Lab provides a concrete basis for institutional conversations without establishing that every possible institutional application has already been demonstrated.
          </p>
          <a href="/our-work" class="btn-primary">Explore the Venture Readiness Lab</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- H. FOUNDER EXPERIENCE & I. SCOPE -->
  <section class="bg-porcelain chapter chapter-moderate-spacing" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--color-strong-boundary);">
    <div class="container grid-12">
      <!-- Founder Experience -->
      <div class="col-12 md-col-6 padding-right-md border-right-md" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);">
        <span class="voice-3">Founder experience</span>
        <h2 class="voice-1" style="font-size: 1.75rem; margin-bottom: var(--space-md);">Experience across programs and institutions</h2>
        <div style="display: flex; gap: var(--space-md); align-items: flex-start; margin-bottom: var(--space-md);">
          <div class="editorial-image-container" style="flex-shrink: 0; width: 120px;">
            <img src="/images/ola.jpeg" alt="Olajumoke Michael" class="editorial-image" style="aspect-ratio: 1/1; object-fit: cover; object-position: center top;" />
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="voice-2" style="font-size: 0.9375rem; margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);">
              Ethnoir was founded by Olajumoke Michael, whose professional background spans entrepreneurship-support programs, program strategy and delivery, institutional operations, stakeholder coordination and program learning.
            </p>
            <p class="voice-2" style="font-size: 0.9375rem; color: var(--color-muted-slate);">
              Her experience includes supporting multi-state entrepreneurship programming through Bpeace and serving as Former Program Director, Winston-Salem Women’s Business Center.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <a href="/about" class="link-secondary" style="font-size: 0.875rem;">About Ethnoir &rarr;</a>
      </div>
      
      <!-- Scope -->
      <div class="col-12 md-col-6 padding-left-md">
        <span class="voice-3">Scope</span>
        <h2 class="voice-1" style="font-size: 1.75rem; margin-bottom: var(--space-md);">A focused institutional role</h2>
        <p class="voice-2" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-md);">
          Ethnoir may be a fit when the work materially concerns entrepreneurship, venture development, the conditions of people navigating ventures or questions about how related support is understood and directed.
        </p>
        <p class="voice-2" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-md); color: var(--color-tidal-ink); font-weight: 500;">
          Ethnoir is not a general management consultancy. General strategic planning, organizational restructuring, corporate change management and operational improvement unrelated to entrepreneurship or venture development fall outside its current focus.
        </p>
        <p class="voice-2" style="color: var(--color-muted-slate); font-size: 0.9375rem;">
          Because Ethnoir’s direct organizational evidence is currently strongest in founder-facing work, institutional inquiries begin with careful scoping and a clear assessment of what Ethnoir can responsibly contribute.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- J. HOW AN INQUIRY BEGINS -->
  <section class="bg-tidal-ink chapter chapter-large-spacing">
    <div class="container">
      <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl); max-width: 800px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;">
        <span class="voice-3" style="color: var(--color-quiet-rule);">How an inquiry begins</span>
        <h2 class="voice-1" style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.5rem); color: var(--color-porcelain);">Bring the venture-development question your organization is trying to understand.</h2>
      </div>
      
      <div class="grid-12" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);">
        <div class="col-12 md-col-4" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--color-muted-slate); padding-top: var(--space-sm);">
          <span class="voice-3" style="color: var(--color-porcelain);">1. Describe the challenge</span>
          <p class="voice-2" style="color: var(--color-parchment);">
            Share the question, decision or support issue your organization is working through and the people or ventures it affects.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-12 md-col-4" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--color-muted-slate); padding-top: var(--space-sm);">
          <span class="voice-3" style="color: var(--color-porcelain);">2. Establish the connection</span>
          <p class="voice-2" style="color: var(--color-parchment);">
            Ethnoir will consider its substantive connection to entrepreneurship or venture development and whether Ethnoir’s current abilities are relevant.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-12 md-col-4" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--color-muted-slate); padding-top: var(--space-sm);">
          <span class="voice-3" style="color: var(--color-porcelain);">3. Clarify a useful next step</span>
          <p class="voice-2" style="color: var(--color-parchment);">
            If there appears to be a fit, the next conversation will focus on what needs to be understood, what information is available and what a responsible scope of work might involve.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      
      <div style="text-align: center; max-width: 640px; margin: 0 auto;">
        <p class="voice-2" style="color: var(--color-quiet-rule); margin-bottom: var(--space-lg); font-style: italic;">
          You do not need a fully formed project or a predetermined service before contacting Ethnoir. An exploratory conversation also does not presume that every inquiry will become an engagement.
        </p>
        <div class="actions-group" style="justify-content: center;">
          <a href="/contact" class="btn-primary" style="border-color: var(--color-porcelain); color: var(--color-porcelain);">Discuss a venture-development challenge</a>
          <a href="/our-work" class="link-secondary" style="color: var(--color-porcelain);">View Our Work</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .col-12 { grid-column: span 12; }
  
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .md-col-8 { grid-column: span 8; }
    .md-col-4 { grid-column: span 4; }
    .md-col-7 { grid-column: span 7; }
    .md-col-7-offset { grid-column: 6 / span 7; }
    .md-col-6 { grid-column: span 6; }
